@*
    HomeStats.razor
    Purpose: Headline statistics row on the portfolio home page — one tile per
    UserStats row belonging to the site owner (REQ-UI-049, BRD-30 revised).

    Renders nothing when the owner has no statistics, so an unconfigured site
    degrades to a shorter page rather than an empty grid (mockup "States" note).

    REQ-UI-048 — TrBlazeUI. Every colour and spacing value is a utility class
    resolving to a design token; no literals.

    TrBlazeUI 2.0.2 (TR-022) ships StatTile / StatGroup, so the local
    Card + CardContent + two hand-sized <span>s composite this used to be —
    the very duplication TR-022 was raised about — is gone. StatGroup also
    owns the responsive grid that used to need utilities.css.

    Dependencies: TrBlazeUI StatGroup/StatTile, BlogModels.Models.UserStat
    Usage: <HomeStats Stats="@stats" /> from Pages/BlogPages/Home.razor
*@

@using BlogModels.Models

@if (Stats is not null && Stats.Count > 0)
{
    <section class="py-10" aria-label="Highlights" data-testid="home-stats">
        <StatGroup Columns="4" data-testid="home-stats-grid">
            @foreach (var stat in Stats)
            {
                <StatTile Value="@stat.StatValue"
                          Label="@stat.StatLabel"
                          data-testid="home-stat-card" />
            }
        </StatGroup>
    </section>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The site owner's headline statistics, already in display order.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<UserStat>? Stats { get; set; }
}
